      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway-lock): close fd when writeFile fails after acquiring lock",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `fs.open(lockPath, \"wx\")` succeeded but `handle.writeFile()` failed (e.g. disk full, quota exceeded), the code threw `GatewayLockError` without closing the file handle, leaking a file descriptor.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWrap the write payload in an inner try-catch. On write failure: close the fd, remove the partial lock file, then re-throw so the outer catch can handle it normally.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible change under normal operation. Prevents fd leak on edge-case disk errors.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/infra/gateway-lock.test.ts`: 16/16 passed ✅",
